From aae6cbb8ff19c745c1b40a5bbea59b32e1a8818b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Micha=C5=82=20Iwanicki?= <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:37:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/28] fix(rdv3): wait in BL31 for the whole RMM platform
 token
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Since commit 7953d9aec ("feat(rdv3): add FIRME attestation platform
hooks"), plat_rmmd_get_cca_attest_token() returns -EAGAIN while the RSE
builds the token, and the RMMD passes E_RMM_AGAIN to the RMM. The RMM
calls again at once, and rmm_el3_ifc_get_platform_token() prints
"Failed to get platform token x0 = 0xfffffffffffffffa" on every call.
Each call polls the MHU 10 times, and the RSE takes many of these calls
to build the token, so the RMM UART fills with the error during boot.
The RMM reaches this request once BL31 returns the realm attestation
key, which needs "fix(mhu): block while waiting for the rest of a
reply".

Fetch the token with cca_attestation_get_plat_token(), which retries
the PSA call until the RSE replies, as RD-V3 did before that commit and
as the realm attestation key request does. The FIRME hooks keep their
non-blocking path.

Signed-off-by: Michał Iwanicki <michal.iwanicki@3mdeb.com>
---
 .../platform/rdv3/rdv3_plat_attest_token.c        | 15 ++++++---------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_plat_attest_token.c b/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_plat_attest_token.c
index 565ca122a..8e98d7980 100644
--- a/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_plat_attest_token.c
+++ b/plat/arm/board/neoverse_rd/platform/rdv3/rdv3_plat_attest_token.c
@@ -5,10 +5,10 @@
  */
 
 #include <assert.h>
-#include <errno.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 #include <string.h>
 
+#include <cca_attestation.h>
 #include <common/debug.h>
 #include <delegated_attestation.h>
 #include <initial_attestation.h>
@@ -216,23 +216,20 @@ uintptr_t firme_plat_shared_buf_addr(firme_instance_e instance,
 int plat_rmmd_get_cca_attest_token(uintptr_t buf, size_t *len, uintptr_t hash,
 				   size_t hash_size, size_t *remaining_size)
 {
-	size_t token_len = 0U;
 	psa_status_t ret;
 
 	assert(*len == SZ_4K);
 
-	ret = rse_delegated_attest_get_token((const uint8_t *)hash, hash_size,
-					     (uint8_t *)buf, *len, &token_len);
-	if (ret == PSA_OPERATION_INCOMPLETE) {
-		return -EAGAIN;
-	}
-
+	/*
+	 * Wait in BL31 until the RSE returns the whole token. The RMM prints
+	 * an error for every E_RMM_AGAIN before it calls again.
+	 */
+	ret = cca_attestation_get_plat_token(buf, len, hash, hash_size);
 	if (ret != PSA_SUCCESS) {
 		ERROR("Unable to fetch CCA attestation token\n");
 		return -1;
 	}
 
-	*len = token_len;
 	assert(*len <= SZ_4K);
 
 	*remaining_size = 0;
-- 
